*2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 533.33 seconds<sup>16,000f</sup>, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since the threatening peons all have a limited spawn, it is possible to outlast the waves of Zang Roos and Zir Zeals before taking on the boss. Bringing a [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] is recommended here, as every enemy present is a zombie and can burrow (with the exception of Inumusha himself). Do not push too hard, as the Doge Base present will fire off a very powerful wave attack if you do and will wipe out your entire army unless they are immune to waves.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] - Very powerful anti-zombie meatshield that can almost solo the stage, can survive a hit from Inumusha and tank the peon waves. Requires research combos to be spammable, however.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] - Able to block the waves released by the Doge Base if you push too hard and set it off, preventing all of your units from dying.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] - Very good crowd control unit against zombie, with a 50% chance to slow them and with an extremely wide LD range. She can also gain [[Savage Blow]] with talents.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] - Only available once you beat a relatively difficult [[Water Conservancy (Merciless)|advent stage]], but is an extremely potent anti-zombie attacker in 4 crown difficulty.
*[[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] - In [[True Form]], fills a very similar role to Cadaver BearCat if you dont have them. They are also part of the "Freeze" Effect UP [[Mystery Club (Combo)]].
*[[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Whale Cat]] - Great anti-zombie tank and attacker, greatly helps against peons similarly to the aforementioned two, while also having much higher health, being able to take 5 hits from Inumusha at level 40 and biting back. Since it tends to knock the boss back to the base, Octopus makes for a great partner.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] - Thanks to his wave immunity and decent damage, a stack of him can easily push the boss backwards without any problem, and keep the boss there without any issues. Keep in mind that the supporting zombies may burrow past it and damage your base while the waves will cripple your units though.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Bloody Jack]] - His naturally high damage, fast attack rate, and anti-zombie knockback means that he can perma-stun Inumunsha once he gets within range.
*[[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION Ubers]] - Every single one of them is quite good against Zombies, so they should at least do something here.
*[[Wrathful Poseidon (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant Poseidon]] - A ranged rusher with high damage, Zombie Killer, and Freeze against Zombies greatly helps with quelling the peon waves.
*[[Baby Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Aegis Garu]] - With resistance to Traited and high damage, Garu is able to tank every enemy in the stage, and his Mini-Waves can snipe Inumusha, and even kill him outright with enough chip damage. He is also Immune to Waves, and can hold the line if the Doge Base gets an attack off.

